rec.games.hack's own quale@uhura.cs.wisc.edu (Douglas E. Quale) said:
-
-I don't have any suggestions for fixing either of this problems directly,
-but how about a couple of new artifacts: longbow of ______ and crossbow
-of _________.  I'll let someone else give them aesthetic names.  The bows
-would turn the arrows/bolts into magic missile, fire or lightning attacks.

Sort of an idea, but...here's my suggestion (like the whetstone ideas, these
are off the top of my head, and not checked for play balance yet):

Bows (crossbows/slings) come in the following flavors:
	Normal
	Elvish	(extra damage vs Orcs? - In any case, stays the same.)
	Orcish  (extra damage vs Elves? - In any case, stays the same.)
	Giant   (normal bow, but need to be 18+ Str to use.  Would add 
		 more to damage.)
	Strength (a magic, giant bow that anyone can use.  a cursed 
		  Bow of Strength would be like shooting feathers.)
	Accuracy (All shots hit for normal damage.  Blessed may do more
		  damage; a cursed bow would always miss.)
	Speed   (Double number of shots.  Blessed would triple or quadruple.
		 Cursed, of course, slows you down by 1/3 or 1/2.)
	Wanding (the arrow continues on its course until it hits a wall.
		 It'll go through any creatures it hits (doing normal damage).)
	Defending (No special benefit, except that it does Hand to Hand damage
		   as a club.)

Arrows (bolts) come in the following flavors:
	Normal
	Elvish	(see above comments)
	Orcish	(see above comments)
	Fire 	(like a wand of fire; watch out for (ahem) backfires)
	Lighting (like a lightning bolt; as above, without the ahem)
	Healing (oh baby, shoot me some more...cursed healing arrows would
		 do damage to whoever they hit.)
	Slaying (arrows coated with that deadly killer bee poison)

Hopefully the magic arrows would only work when fired from a bow; it would
make using bows an advantage.  Especially when you get your Arrows of Slaying
firing out of your Bow of Accuracy.

The magic arrows would never be recoverable, otherwise it gets ridiculous.

And then there's the necessary question to ask: What advantages do bows have
now, that makes them better than throwing arrows?

Enough for now...I'm sure the Nethack team is still trying to figure out
whether wetstones are worth the trouble...

